// The declared schema, as JSON Schema and back.
//
// ONE projection with two consumers, which is the whole reason it is a package
// rather than a function inside either of them: the universal UI generates a
// form from it, and the agent runtime generates a tool's `parameters` from it.
// Two implementations would drift, and they would drift in the direction of
// the form accepting what the tool rejects.
//
// Pure and target-agnostic like statedef/ and viewgen/: a SchemaInfo in, a
// Json out, and no host, no bundle, no wasm. That is what lets it describe a
// HOST component as readily as a guest one — the declared shape is the same
// shape, and only the docs a manifest carries are extra.
import {
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/core" @tutuca,
  "moonbitlang/core/json",
  "moonbitlang/core/debug",
}

import {
  "moonbitlang/core/test",
} for "test"
